[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ShopResource" load_steps=12 format=3 uid="uid://cmbrvlshopgoods"]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopResource.cs" id="1_shop"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopStockEntry.cs" id="2_entry"]
[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://data/loot/ShopLeveledGear.tres" id="3_leveled"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopInvestmentTier.cs" id="4_tier"]

; The first shop (Phase 38A, stocked properly in 38B): the Ember Crown's general goods. Consumables
; and common materials rather than gear — a merchant who sold weapons outright would be competing with
; loot and crafting for the same job, and DESIGN §6 is explicit that gold buys convenience, never
; defining power. What gear this stall does carry comes out of the leveled pool below, rolled and
; scarce, which is a different promise from a shelf you can shop off.
;
; The spread is 1.5 / 0.4, so selling something back costs you roughly two thirds of its price. That
; gap is the point: it makes looting-to-sell a slow income rather than a loop, and it is the number
; Phase 56 balance will actually tune.
;
; Stock split three ways on purpose, which is exactly what 38B is for:
;   - Potions and herbs are FINITE. A player cannot stand at the stall and out-heal a region; they buy
;     what is there and come back. RestockDays = 1 is what makes that a wait rather than a wall.
;   - Ore and scrap are UNLIMITED (Quantity = 0). A materials stall running out of iron ore would only
;     make crafting feel gated on a shopping trip, and there is nothing interesting about that.
;   - The leveled pool is ROLLED at each restock and scales with the player's level.
;
; 38C: Aldreth is a villager, so FactionId prices by faction.villagers standing — Allied buys at 15%
; off, Unfriendly pays 15% over, and at or below the villagers' HostileThreshold he refuses to deal at
; all. PurseGold is the other half of that phase: 250 gold is enough to fence a decent haul and not
; enough to fence a field of corpses, and it refills with the shelves on the same one-day clock. Note
; BuyMarkup must stay far enough above 1 for the discount to have room — at 1.5 every tier is distinct,
; and --validate rejects a markup that bottoms out at Honored.
;
; 38F: Aldreth authors NO AcceptedTags and NO Specialties, and that is his whole identity rather than an
; omission. A general store is the merchant who takes everything and knows nothing especially well — he
; will buy the pelts Bryn refuses and the ruby nobody in town has a use for, and he pays plainly for all
; of it. That is a real decision the player makes every time their pack fills up: walk across the square
; for a better price, or empty the whole bag here.
; ⚠️ A settlement needs one merchant like this or loot becomes unsellable by authoring accident. In the
; Ember Crown that is Aldreth, and it stays that way until 38L's market district gives the specialists
; enough coverage between them.
;
; 38E turns the three town_hub stub vendors into real shops. Until then:
; `shop shop.ember_crown.goods` in the F1 console, `shop restock shop.ember_crown.goods` to skip the
; wait, and `rep faction.villagers <delta>` to walk the discount up and down.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_potion"]
script = ExtResource("2_entry")
ItemId = "item.potion.health"
Quantity = 5

